From: harness-dft project
Subject: [PATCH] PHonon/PH: fix missing comma in symmetry-op FORMAT string

phq_summary.f90's verbose symmetry-operation printout crashes ph.x with a
Fortran runtime I/O error ("Missing comma between descriptors") whenever it
prints a symmetry operation with a nonzero fractional translation (a
non-symmorphic operation) -- i.e. whenever `ft(:,isym)` is nonzero. This is
common for `ibrav=0` cells (arbitrary CELL_PARAMETERS, e.g. anything built
from an ASE/pymatgen/AiiDA StructureData rather than a recognized Bravais
lattice), which is exactly why QE's own `pw.x` "using ibrav=0 with symmetry
is DISCOURAGED" warning is not just cosmetic for ph.x.

The WRITE statement at the top of that print block is missing a comma
between the repeated numeric edit descriptor `3(i6,5x)` and the following
character-literal descriptor -- every sibling WRITE in the same subroutine
(the s(2,...)/s(3,...) continuation lines immediately below it, and the
equivalent block with no fractional translation) has the comma; this one
line does not.

Confirmed via: a debug rebuild (plain gfortran, -O0) reproducing a clear,
human-readable compiler error naming this exact line, and a full rebuild
with the one-line fix applied completing an otherwise-crashing DFPT run
(2-atom hexagonal ibrav=0 cell, 4-qpoint mesh) to completion with correct,
physically sane phonon frequencies. Not previously suspected to be a
compiler-toolchain or ScaLAPACK/MPI-configuration issue, despite crash
signatures (a libgfortran `data_transfer_init` I/O-layer segfault-style
abort) that superficially resembled one.

Reported against Quantum ESPRESSO 7.5, PHonon/PH/phq_summary.f90.

--- a/PHonon/PH/phq_summary.f90
+++ b/PHonon/PH/phq_summary.f90
@@ -186,7 +186,7 @@
            ft1 = at(1,1)*ft(1,isym) + at(1,2)*ft(2,isym) + at(1,3)*ft(3,isym)
            ft2 = at(2,1)*ft(1,isym) + at(2,2)*ft(2,isym) + at(2,3)*ft(3,isym)
            ft3 = at(3,1)*ft(1,isym) + at(3,2)*ft(2,isym) + at(3,3)*ft(3,isym)
-           WRITE(stdout, '(1x,"cryst.",3x,"s(",i2,") = (",3(i6,5x) &
+           WRITE(stdout, '(1x,"cryst.",3x,"s(",i2,") = (",3(i6,5x), &
                 &                    " )    f =( ",f10.7," )")') isymq,  &
                 & (s(1,ipol,isym), ipol = 1, 3), ft(1,isym)
            WRITE(stdout, '(17x," (",3(i6,5x), &
